Z||000001||Back On Holiday||10-06-2001||02:42 PM||||First off, Welcome to the List.<P>As for problems, ANY Car you buy has problems - Even BRAND-NEW cars have problems.<P>I had an 82' Buick skylark once, and it always had something going wrong with it, I miss that car and wish I kept it.<BR>I also had a '79 ford Pinto sw, and it had less problems than the skylark, but I PREFERED the skylark....don't ask me why.<P>something to consider, 2.5 L4 vs 2.8 v6<BR>each has its own problems, also year matters.  some prefer the 84, or 88 2.5's (and the ones in between) and some only like 88' 2.8's. (and the other 2.8 years)<P>and the last...Price!  You may get a nice v6 you may not need to work on for awhile for a hefty price, or you can get a junker real cheap and fix her up good as new.<P>just my opinion...nobody flame me!<BR><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||1
